# Deploy Next.js Website Live on sathwarainfotech.com

Deploy the cloned Next.js application at `/var/www/html/sathwarainfotech.com/si-website` on the live domain `sathwarainfotech.com` (using port 9003 internally via PM2 and Nginx reverse proxy).

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **DNS Configuration Required**: The domain `sathwarainfotech.com` currently points to Hostinger parking IPs (`2.57.91.252`, `88.222.222.192`). 
> You must point the **A record** for `sathwarainfotech.com` and `www.sathwarainfotech.com` to this server's public IP: **`72.62.135.9`** in your domain registrar (Hostinger) settings.
> 
> Once the DNS points to this server, we will run Certbot to configure SSL/HTTPS automatically.

## Proposed Changes

### Next.js Application Setup

1. **Install Dependencies**: Run `npm install` inside `/var/www/html/sathwarainfotech.com/si-website`.
2. **Build Application**: Run `npm run build` inside the same directory to build the production build.
3. **PM2 Process**: Start the application on port `9003` and name it `sathwarainfotech-com`.
   - Command: `pm2 start npm --name "sathwarainfotech-com" -- start -- -p 9003 -H 0.0.0.0`
   - Save configuration: `pm2 save`

### Nginx Configuration

#### [NEW] [sathwarainfotech.com](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/sathwarainfotech.com)
Create a new Nginx server configuration pointing to port `9003`.

```nginx
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name sathwarainfotech.com www.sathwarainfotech.com;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://localhost:9003;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection 'upgrade';
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_cache_bypass $http_upgrade;
    }
}
```

Enable this site by creating a symlink:
`ln -s /etc/nginx/sites-available/sathwarainfotech.com /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/`

Verify Nginx syntax:
`nginx -t`

Reload Nginx:
`systemctl reload nginx`

## Verification Plan

### Automated/Manual Verification
- Verify that Nginx config is successfully reloaded.
- Check PM2 status: `pm2 status` should show `sathwarainfotech-com` online.
- Check local website response: `curl -I http://localhost:9003` to verify that Next.js is serving pages.
- List of commands run will be shared with the user.
